00:15:46,610 --> 00:15:48,820
Hmm. Oh, Mindy.

254
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:51,090
Oh, you are so stupid.

255
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:55,110
Oh, we are both so stupid.

256
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:56,660
What do you mean?

257
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:01,700
- Smell familiar?     - Oh, no.

258
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:03,210
Mm-hm.

259
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,380
Oh, I'm so sorry.

260
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:08,340
Oh, no, me. I am so sorry.

261
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,840
No, I am sorry. I'm sorry.

262
00:16:24,730 --> 00:16:26,400
Oh, my.

263
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,980
Four letters, "circle or hoop."

264
00:16:31,150 --> 00:16:32,530
Ring, damn it, ring.

265
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,240
Thanks.

266
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,780
You know our phone's not working?

267
00:16:38,950 --> 00:16:40,450
What?

268
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:44,410
I tried to call you from the coffee shop. There was no answer.

269
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,210
I turned it off.

270
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,960
Mother of God, I turned it off.

271
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:50,630
Just like you told her you did.

272
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,720
Just pointing out the irony.

273
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:58,430
So listen, I went across the street and talked to the doorman.

274
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:01,390
I got the peeper's name. Can I use the phone?

275
00:17:03,810 --> 00:17:05,480
Can I use your phone?

276
00:17:09,230 --> 00:17:11,900
Yeah, the number for a Sidney Marks, please.

277
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:13,820
"Heating device."

278
00:17:14,990 --> 00:17:16,200
Radiator.

279
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:17,990
Five letters.

280
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,820
"Rdtor."

281
00:17:24,370 --> 00:17:26,620
Yeah, is Sidney there?

282
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:28,880
Oh, this is?

283
00:17:29,170 --> 00:17:31,960
- Sidney's a woman.     - So she's a woman, so what?

284
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:34,460
Yeah, yeah, so what?

285
00:17:34,630 --> 00:17:36,340
Look, I live across the street...

286
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:38,800
...and I know all about you and your telescope.

287
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:40,930
And I don't appreciate it, okay?

288
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,890
Yeah, I can see you right now. Hello?

289
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:47,190
Look, if I wanna walk around my apartment in my underwear...

290
00:17:47,350 --> 00:17:50,770
...I shouldn't have to feel like... Thank you.

291
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,070
That's not really the point.

292
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,860
The point is, that...

293
00:17:57,030 --> 00:17:59,910
- Mostly free-weights, but occasionally...     - Joey.

294
00:18:01,990 --> 00:18:04,660
Yeah, my neighbor. Yeah, the brunette.

295
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:09,350
She said you looked pretty that day in the green dress.

296
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,500
The green dress? Really?

297
00:18:12,670 --> 00:18:15,340
She said you looked like Ingrid Bergman that day.

298
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:18,050
Heh. No.

299
00:18:23,220 --> 00:18:24,310
- Hey.     - Hey.

300
00:18:24,470 --> 00:18:26,270
- You got a second?     - Sure, sure.

301
00:18:26,430 --> 00:18:27,890
Come on...

302
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:29,350
...in.

303
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,810
Hello, sweetheart.

304
00:18:31,690 --> 00:18:36,400
- What you guys doing here?     - Uh, we are here to break up with you.

305
00:18:37,690 --> 00:18:38,900
Both of you?

306
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:43,320
We think you're a horrible human being, and bad things should happen to you.

307
00:18:45,990 --> 00:18:48,120
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. God, I am so sorry.

308
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:50,750
I'm an idiot. I was weak. I couldn't help myself.

309
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:54,000
Whatever I did, I only did because I love you so much.

310
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:58,760
Uh, which one of us are you talking to there, Bar?

311
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:00,550
Um...

312
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:02,930
Mindy.

313
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,810
Mindy, of course, Mindy. It was always Mindy.

314
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:08,870
Even when we were having sex in that chair?

315
00:19:08,890 --> 00:19:12,350
I swear, look, whatever I was doing, I was always thinking of you.

316
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,400
Oh, please.

317
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:17,940
During that second time, you couldn't have picked her out of a lineup.

318
00:19:18,110 --> 00:19:19,190
You did it twice?

319
00:19:19,530 --> 00:19:22,820
Well, the first time didn't really count. You know, it was Barry.

320
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:24,700
Oh, right.

321
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,830
Honey, baby, sweetheart, look...

322
00:19:26,990 --> 00:19:28,910
Just give me another chance, okay?

323
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:32,120
We'll start all over again. We'll go back to Aruba.

324
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,290
What do you say?

325
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:38,420
Dr. Farber, we've got an emergency here.

326
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:41,220
Jason Castalano's choking on his retainer.

327
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:44,260
Oh, God. Uh, I'll be right there, Bernice.

328
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:46,720
Look, please, please don't go anywhere, okay?

329
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:50,060
- I'll be right back.     - Okay.

330
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:53,230
Okay, and we'll be here, hating you.

331
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:57,150
See how he was sweating when he walked out of here?

332
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:59,690
If I'm hogging the ball, you jump right in there...

333
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:03,570
...and take a couple of punches. Because I'm telling you, this feels great.

334
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:07,620
Yeah, I'm pretty sure I'm still gonna marry him.

335
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:10,910
What are you talking about?

336
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:13,870
Mindy, the guy is the devil.

337
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,210
He is Satan in a smock.

338
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,880
Look, I know he's not perfect.

339
00:20:22,550 --> 00:20:24,970
But the truth is, at the end of the day...

340
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:27,600
...I still really wanna be...

341
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:31,390
...Mrs. Dr. Barry Farber...

342
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:33,680
...D.D.S.

343
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:35,850
Oh, God.

344
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:39,730
I hope you can find some way to be happy for me.

345
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:42,860
And I hope you'll still be my maid of honor.

346
00:20:43,610 --> 00:20:46,700
And I hope Barry doesn't kill you and eat you in Aruba.

347
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,500
You okay?

348
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,290
Yeah.

349
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:59,590
Really?

350
00:21:00,170 --> 00:21:01,590
Yeah.

351
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:04,510
You know, ever since I ran out on Barry at the wedding...

352
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,640
...I have wondered whether I made the right choice.

353
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,050
Oh. And now I know.

354
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:12,850
I'm so glad.

355
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:18,770
Big day.

356
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:30,620
All right, I'll give you this: Mr. Peanut is a better dresser.

357
00:21:30,780 --> 00:21:33,830
I mean, he's got the monocle, he's got the top hat...

358
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,870
Did you know he's gay?

359
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:43,090
I just wanna clarify this. Are you outing Mr. Peanut?

360
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:47,050
- Chandler?     - Danielle, hi.

361
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:49,760
Everybody, this is Danielle. Danielle, everybody.

362
00:21:49,930 --> 00:21:51,140
Hi.

363
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,720
- What are you doing here?     - I've been calling you...

364
00:21:53,890 --> 00:21:55,930
...but it turns out I had your number wrong.

365
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:59,440
And when I finally got the right one from Information, there was no answer.

366
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:02,610
So I thought I'd just come down here and make sure you were okay.

367
00:22:02,770 --> 00:22:05,400
Oh, uh, I'm okay.

368
00:22:05,570 --> 00:22:08,110
Listen, uh, maybe we could get together later?

369
00:22:08,610 --> 00:22:11,620
That sounds good. I'll call you. Or you call me, whatever.

370
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:12,950
- You know.     - Ha, ha.

371
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:14,490
- You got it.     - Okay.

372
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:16,580
- Bye, everybody.     - Bye.

373
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:20,040
Woo-hoo! Yeah, there you go.

374
00:22:20,210 --> 00:22:22,000
Second date.

375
00:22:22,170 --> 00:22:23,920
I don't know.

376
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:25,300
You don't know?

377
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:29,220
Oh, she seems nice, but that thing about her coming all the way here...

378
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:33,300
...just to see if I was okay? I mean, how needy is that?

